    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 12000,
      "caption": "Among routes to the same prefix, a fixed tie-break ladder decides.",
      "narration": "For the same prefix, the decision process compares highest LOCAL_PREF, shortest AS_PATH, lowest ORIGIN, lowest MED, eBGP over iBGP, lowest IGP cost, and finally router ID.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Decision ladder",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "l",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "1 highest LOCAL_PREF",
            "2 shortest AS_PATH",
            "3 lowest ORIGIN, then MED",
            "4 eBGP over iBGP",
            "5 lowest IGP cost to next hop",
            "6 lowest router ID"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "f",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "l",
          "at": 8000,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "LOCAL_PREF encodes business: customer routes beat peers beat providers.",
      "narration": "Operators set LOCAL_PREF per neighbour, so money decides first: prefer customers, then peers, then paid transit. AS_PATH length is only the second tiebreaker.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Policy first",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "customer route\nLOCAL_PREF 300",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "pop"
        },
        {
          "id": "p",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "peer route\nLOCAL_PREF 200",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 42,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "color": "blue",
          "at": 1500,
          "enter": "pop"
        },
        {
          "id": "t",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "transit route\nLOCAL_PREF 100",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 62,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "color": "gray",
          "at": 2500,
          "enter": "pop"
        },
        {
          "id": "f",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "c",
          "at": 6000,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 11000,
      "caption": "A leak re-announces routes it should not; unfiltered neighbours accept them.",
      "narration": "A leak or hijack announces routes the origin never authorised. In 2008 Pakistan Telecom announced a more specific YouTube prefix, and longest prefix match pulled traffic in.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Hijacks and leaks",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "o",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "Legit /22",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 38,
          "h": 10,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "pop"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "Bogus /24",
          "x": 54,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 38,
          "h": 10,
          "color": "red",
          "at": 1500,
          "enter": "pop"
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The /24 wins by longest-prefix match, then spreads upstream if nobody filters it.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 42,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 3500,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "m",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Leaks need an unfiltered upstream to spread.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 66,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 6500,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Defences: RPKI origin validation, ROA maxLength, and strict prefix filters.",
      "narration": "Defences are RPKI route origin validation, tight maxLength in ROAs, and prefix filters on customers. They only work if upstream networks enforce them.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Defences",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
